First, we define the protocol buffer. This allows the client to send a playbook path and receive a stream of log lines.

```protobuf
// playbook.proto
syntax = "proto3";

package playbook;

// Represents a single line of output from Ansible
message LogLine {
  string timestamp = 1;
  string level = 2; // e.g., "INFO", "ERROR", "PLAY"
  string message = 3;
}

// Request to start a playbook
message RunRequest {
  string playbook_path = 1;
  map<string, string> extra_vars = 2;
}

// Response stream
message RunResponse {
  LogLine log = 1;
  bool finished = 2;
}

// Service definition
service PlaybookService {
  // Unary call to start the playbook
  rpc Run(PlaybookService.RunRequest) returns (stream PlaybookService.RunResponse);
}
```

